course: dictionary
lesson: 12640
title: Dispensed: given out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The machine dispensed a cold drink after I pushed the button.» Look at the clues: a machine, a button, and a drink that comes out. So dispensed must mean given out or handed out.
explain: Dispensed can also mean prepared and handed out as medicine. «The pharmacist dispensed the medicine carefully.» A pharmacist is a trained person who prepares medicine, so dispensed here means prepared and given out.
explain: Watch for «dispensed with». «We dispensed with the lift because we only needed to go up one floor.» Dispensed with means did without, because it was not needed. Test it by swapping in did without: «We did without the lift» still makes sense.
fact: Dispensed is the past form of dispense, which means to give out.
fact: A machine can dispense drinks, cash, soap or tickets.
fact: A pharmacist dispenses medicine from a doctor's prescription, so only trained people should do it.
fact: «Dispensed with» means got rid of something or did without it because it was not needed.
fact: In formal writing, «dispensed justice» means someone in charge gave out a judgement.
exercise: «The machine dispensed three sweets each time.» What does dispensed mean here? | Ate | Stole | *Gave out | Hid away
exercise: «The pharmacist dispensed the medicine carefully.» Who dispensed the medicine? | *A pharmacist | A football | A bus driver | A dog
exercise: «We dispensed with the lift because we only needed one floor.» What does dispensed with mean here? | Broke the lift | Asked a friend for a lift | *Did without it | Bought a new lift
test: «Only an adult or a pharmacist should dispense medicine.» Why? | *Because medicine must be handed out safely by a trained person | Because medicine should be thrown away | Because medicine is always free | Because medicine tastes nice
test: «The judge dispensed justice fairly in the court.» What does dispensed justice mean? | *Gave out a fair decision | Lost the case | Ran away from the court | Paid a big fine
exam: «We dispensed with the car and walked to school.» Which meaning of dispensed is this? | *Got rid of it, or did without it | Fixed the car | Sold the car to a friend | Gave out a car
